# The Monolith of Light, made in the voxel editor by hand: the camera
# framed on an open patch of ground, then a blue plinth, white lanterns,
# a golden spire and a ruby crown, every voxel placed with a click and
# held here by the volume's words; the picture at the end by its colours.
# Coordinates come from the editor's own camera (eye_at, forward,
# ray_at): each click aims at the middle of the face it builds on.
# A frame every tenth of a second, so the Player, which plays a replay
# at its own times (orla-player --replay), shows it at a pace to watch.
scene voxel.osn
window 960 540 1
frame 0.0

# Tilt: the middle button dragged down 25 pixels, 0.2 more pitch.
pointer 700 120 up
frame 0.1
button middle down
frame 0.2
pointer 700 145 up
frame 0.3
button middle up
frame 0.4
expect state.result[0].pitch = 0.700 0.001

# Closer: the wheel, three times.
wheel 0 1
frame 0.5
wheel 0 0
frame 0.6
wheel 0 1
frame 0.7
wheel 0 0
frame 0.8
wheel 0 1
frame 0.9
wheel 0 0
frame 1.0
expect state.result[0].zoom = 0.560 0.001

# Pan with Shift and the middle button, -29.4 and -327.3 pixels, to bring
# the patch of ground at the site to the middle of the picture.
pointer 400.0 200.0 up
key 16 down
frame 1.1
button middle down
frame 1.2
pointer 370.6 -127.3 up
frame 1.3
button middle up
frame 1.4
key 16 up
frame 1.5
expect state.result[0].pan = 6.830 -10.800 6.140 0.01
# The colour item, clicked 3 time(s): white to blue.
pointer 518.0 508.0 down
frame 1.6
pointer up
frame 1.7
pointer 518.0 508.0 down
frame 1.8
pointer up
frame 1.9
pointer 518.0 508.0 down
frame 2.0
pointer up
frame 2.1
expect state.result[0].colour = 4

